 Z←CalculatePlanets OBSERVER;DATE;PLANETS;AA;MN;SN;KO;K;PHASE;VP;AAE;PLANETCOORD
⍝ Calculates positions of sun, moon, planets, and comet
⍝ OBSERVER is LAT,DATE,TIME
⍝ Z is PLANETS AA VP PLANETCOORD PHASE AAE
 DATE←OBSERVER[2]
 PLANETS←DATE EARTHVIEW DATE PLANETPOS(3≠⍳9)⌿Data.planets
 SN←DATE EARTHVIEW 1 3⍴0 0 0
 K←100≥|DATE-JNU 12 28 1973
 KO←DATE EARTHVIEW(DATE/⍨K)COMETPOS Data.kohoutek
 MN←MOONPOS DATE
 PHASE←MN[1;1]MOONPHASE SN[1;1]
 PLANETS←MN,[1]SN,[1]PLANETS,[1]KO
 MN←MN[;3]PARALLAXADJUST OBSERVER SKYPOS MN[;1 2]
 AA←MN,[1]OBSERVER SKYPOS 1 0↓PLANETS
 PLANETCOORD←MAPCARTESIAN PROJECTION AAE←(VP←VISIBLE AA)⌿AA
 Z←PLANETS AA VP PLANETCOORD PHASE AAE
